Graph: SDD

Purpose:
  Engineering Knowledge Graph and Traceability Engine. Connects
  all .sdd system elements into a single traceable engineering
  model. Graph stores relationships, indexes, traces, and impact
  — NOT copies of source files.

Owns: ./

Modes:
  IMPLEMENT — task implementation context
  DEBUG     — incident debugging context
  SECURITY  — security analysis context
  SUPPORT   — support/troubleshooting context
  AUDIT     — full traceability audit

Rules:
  [GR1]  Graph stores relationships, NOT copies of source files.
  [GR2]  Every major object is a node with standardized ID.
  [GR3]  Every relationship uses standard relation types.
  [GR4]  Task execution order comes from dependency graph, NOT task ID.
  [GR5]  Graph MUST detect cycles (TASK-CYCLE).
  [GR6]  Graph MUST support forward and reverse impact analysis.
  [GR7]  Graph MUST calculate blast radius for changes.
  [GR8]  Graph MUST track coverage (BDD, Unit, Integration, Security, etc.).
  [GR9]  Graph MUST detect drift between .sdd and source.
  [GR10] Graph MUST detect untraceable changes.
  [GR11] Decision history MUST be preserved (SUPERSEDES).
  [GR12] Graph MUST support scale-aware analysis.

ReadOrder:
   1  @model.sdd

Navigation:
  Graph: @graph/INDEX.sdd
  Model: @graph/model.sdd
  ProjectGraph: @projects/{project_name}/graph/INDEX.sdd

State: +